1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,160
<i>Have you never felt anything for me?</i>

2
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,360
You're my client.

3
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,600
<i>Then when you kissed me and slept with me,</i>

4
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,320
<i>was all of it just for work?</i>

5
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,960
Rakkhun is hurting
because of you right now.

6
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:17,600
Rakkhun loves you.

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,120
Vann!

8
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:23,400
I want to be your boyfriend.

9
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,760
<i>Rakkhun, will you be my boyfriend?</i>

10
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,920
<i>You're going to sing here?</i>

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,160
I'm offering myself
to test things out first.

12
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,439
If we end up in the same band,

13
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,120
<i>we'll know whether our voices</i>
<i>work well together.</i>

14
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:35,920
Okay?

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,520
<i>I’ve been looking at you for so long</i>

16
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,200
<i>I don't dare to look</i>

17
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:18,640
<i>I always have to avoid your eyes</i>

18
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:22,760
<i>I’m afraid that one day</i>

19
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:26,480
<i>If you find out</i>

20
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:31,160
<i>The truth I’ve been hiding away</i>

21
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:37,120
<i>The secret I’ve hidden</i>
<i>I’ve never told anyone</i>

22
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:42,160
<i>I don't think I can hold it back anymore</i>

23
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:49,160
<i>The closer I am to you,</i>
<i>The more I want to reveal my heart</i>

24
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:54,120
<i>When we make eye contact</i>
<i>My heart shakes even more</i>

25
00:01:54,200 --> 00:02:00,080
<i>It’s just too hard</i>
<i>To keep this love hidden away</i>

26
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,760
<i>And the secret inside your heart</i>
<i>Does it include me at all?</i>

27
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:12,680
<i>Please tell me what’s in your heart</i>
<i>Let me know</i>

28
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,360
See?

29
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,320
See how well we sing together?

30
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,720
Please audition for our band.

31
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:31,720
What do you say? Can you do it for me?

32
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,480
Phatee, you're the first person
I've ever begged like this.

33
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,000
<i>Phatee!</i>

34
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,480
<i>Phatee!</i>

35
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,320
Phatee!

36
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,040
Phatee!

37
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,600
Phatee!

38
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:05,920
Damn.

39
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,040
I thought you were fucking dead.
I've been calling you forever.

40
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,840
What do you want?

41
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:14,000
Linda sent me to get you.
Looks like there's a job.

42
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,360
I'll be there.

43
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,600
Okay.

44
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,880
It was just a dream.

45
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,840
Why did it feel so damn good?

46
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,160
PJ, add the keyboard sync this time.

47
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,240
I'll handle it.

48
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,920
I'll add the bass.

49
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,920
Got it.

50
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,960
Let's rehearse one more time.

51
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,240
Come on, Saw.

52
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,200
That's enough for today.

53
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,360
Kao.

54
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,880
We booked the rehearsal room
until this evening.

55
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,280
Check the system first.

56
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,080
I canceled your rehearsal room myself.

57
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,760
What do you mean?

58
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:26,240
Someone needs the rehearsal room more.

59
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,640
They're a new group of trainees

60
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,880
scheduled to debut next week.

61
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,920
So I had to let them
use the rehearsal room first.

62
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,960
You guys can head over there.

63
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,560
Kao.

64
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,840
We've been waiting to debut for ages too.

65
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,480
I already told you.

66
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:49,640
If you still can't find a main vocalist
with a distinctive voice,

67
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,360
I don't see why you should debut.

68
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,280
There's no selling point.

69
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:57,080
You guys can leave now. Go.

70
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,360
Wait until they're gone,
then you can start rehearsing.

71
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,840
Fuck!

72
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,920
Don't take it out on me.

73
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,200
I think

74
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,480
if this keeps up,

75
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,120
we won't just lose rehearsal time.

76
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,480
They might even stop us from using
the rehearsal room altogether.

77
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,200
Exactly.

78
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:42,160
What about that great guy you said
you want in the band?

79
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:45,640
What did he say? If he doesn't join,
we'll have to change the plan.

80
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,280
No.

81
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,600
Trust me.

82
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:53,840
This time, he'll definitely say yes.

83
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,520
Linda, I think I found the client.

84
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,280
The client's name is Cherry, right?

85
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,000
<i>No, her name is Lilly.</i>

86
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,640
<i>Take good care of her.</i>

87
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,720
<i>And smile.</i>

88
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,880
Okay.

89
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:27,240
I'm Phatee from The Crow Club.

90
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,640
You're Lilly, our client, right?

91
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,640
Oh.

92
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:35,320
Yes, but I'm not your client.

93
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:38,080
I'm just the middleman
who contacted The Crow Club.

94
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,400
The one who hired you

95
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,000
is that guy.

96
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:42,760
You.

97
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:46,720
Uh…

98
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,680
Now that you've met, I'll get going.

99
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,600
Hey.

100
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,440
Hey, wait.

101
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,360
Hey, I already paid Linda.

102
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,680
Hey.

103
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,320
I'll have Linda refund you.

104
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,560
Today's job is simple.

105
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,640
I won't ask you to do anything else.

106
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:15,120
But if you want to do something else,

107
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,360
I wouldn't mind.

108
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,000
Hey, I'm kidding.

109
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:22,880
How about this?

110
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:26,200
If you take the job
and go shopping with me today,

111
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,960
I promise

112
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:30,760
I won't bother you
about the audition again.

113
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:34,000
Whatever you decide, it's up to you.

114
00:08:36,679 --> 00:08:37,679
Are you in?

115
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,360
What kind of music
do you usually listen to?

116
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,480
I listen to anything.

117
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:50,960
Rock. Pop rock. Indie rock.

118
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:53,080
What do you mean, anything?
That's all rock.

119
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:56,280
So, do you have a favorite band?

120
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,880
Hey.

121
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,240
You can answer me.

122
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,960
Even if you lie, I won't know.

123
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,600
I have to make some conversation.

124
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,880
Otherwise it'll get awkward.

125
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,240
"Pause."

126
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:15,880
Hey.

127
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,640
You've got good taste.

128
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,880
What's your favorite song?

129
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,400
"Secret."

130
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:36,760
Let's check out this store.

131
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,960
Is this necklace pretty?

132
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,040
It is.

133
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,720
That store has nice clothes too.

134
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,880
Let's go look.

135
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,400
What's your dream?

136
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,840
Where do you want to go,
or what do you want to do?

137
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:59,120
Let's make it simple.
What do you like doing?

138
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,040
Nothing.

139
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,280
If it's what I like doing most,
I guess playing guitar.

140
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,800
Hey. Come here.

141
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,520
I think

142
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:20,520
this shirt would look good on you.

143
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:24,880
Try it on for me.

144
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,920
Please?

145
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,040
Come on, try it on.

146
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,120
I'll help.

147
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,200
I'll do it myself.

148
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,400
Come on. Hurry up.

149
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:07,640
Don't you ever think about
taking music seriously?

150
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:10,040
You don't have to convince me.

151
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,720
Even if you try all day,
you won't succeed.

152
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,000
Huh.

153
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,440
Hey. Hold this shirt up for me.

154
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,400
Come on.

155
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,640
I'll take this one.

156
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,840
I'm really good at this.

157
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,280
You can wear this denim shirt.

158
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,640
You'll look cool.

159
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,600
Cool like me.

160
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,880
Let's go.

161
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,640
Where are you going?

162
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,640
That sounds so damn good.

163
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:05,760
Come here.

164
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,160
Follow me.

165
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,440
What are you doing?

166
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,800
Hey.

167
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:20,960
Come on.

168
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:26,480
The time I hired you for today
isn't up yet, right?

169
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,600
Consider this part of the job.

170
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:32,960
Uh…

171
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,000
Excuse me.

172
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,120
- Can I borrow your guitar?
- Sure.

173
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,880
Thanks.

174
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,880
Here. Take it.

175
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,640
Play whichever song you like best.

176
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,760
I'll follow your lead.

177
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,560
Here, take it.

178
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,800
Like this.

179
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:09,880
Come on.

180
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,400
Hey.

181
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,200
If you don't know where to look,

182
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,880
look at me.

183
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,720
- Hey.
- Yeah?

184
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,480
Can you play the backing track for me?

185
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,560
Sure.

186
00:13:56,080 --> 00:14:00,160
<i>I’ve been looking at you for so long</i>

187
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:06,480
<i>I don't dare to look</i>
<i>I always have to avoid your eyes</i>

188
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:10,800
<i>I’m afraid that one day</i>

189
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:14,280
<i>If you find out</i>

190
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:18,400
<i>the truth I’ve been hiding away</i>

191
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:24,920
<i>The secret I’ve hidden</i>
<i>I’ve never told anyone</i>

192
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,720
<i>I don't think I can hold it back anymore</i>

193
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:34,920
<i>The closer I am to you</i>
<i>The more I want to reveal my heart</i>

194
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:40,200
<i>When we make eye contact</i>
<i>My heart shakes even more</i>

195
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:45,760
<i>It’s just too hard</i>
<i>To keep this love hidden away</i>

196
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:51,520
<i>And the secret inside your heart,</i>
<i>Does it include me at all?</i>

197
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,280
<i>Please tell me</i>

198
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:59,440
<i>What’s in your heart, let me know</i>

199
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:12,120
<i>I take your words</i>

200
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:14,440
<i>And overthink them</i>

201
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:18,440
<i>Secretly imagining things</i>
<i>All by myself like this</i>

202
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:22,920
<i>Because you…</i>
<i>You are just so incredibly good</i>

203
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,160
<i>How much longer</i>

204
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:31,520
<i>Do I have to keep</i>
<i>The words "I love you" inside?</i>

205
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:36,920
<i>The secret I’ve hidden</i>
<i>I’ve never told anyone</i>

206
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,520
<i>I don't think I can hold it back anymore</i>

207
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:46,920
<i>The closer I am to you</i>
<i>The more I want to reveal my heart</i>

208
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,920
<i>When we make eye contact</i>
<i>My heart shakes even more</i>

209
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:57,800
<i>It’s just too hard</i>
<i>To keep this love hidden away</i>

210
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:03,520
<i>And the secret inside your heart</i>
<i>Does it include me at all?</i>

211
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:06,240
<i>Please tell me</i>

212
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:11,720
<i>What’s in your heart, let me know</i>

213
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,400
See? You can do it.

214
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:06,640
Why are you sitting
at the bar today, Mr. Writer?

215
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,359
Don't act like we're close.

216
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,119
You wouldn't take the job
when I asked you to be my boyfriend.

217
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,000
You're awful.

218
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:15,640
When someone hits on you, you reject him.

219
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,280
Then when the guy pursuing
you tries to leave,

220
00:17:19,359 --> 00:17:21,240
you casually pull him back in.

221
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,400
That's not very nice.

222
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:30,680
But it's just like
the protagonist in my novel.

223
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,560
I like that kind of push-and-pull.

224
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:40,480
I just wanted to know
why you're sitting at the bar today.

225
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:44,040
I just wanted a change of perspective.

226
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,320
Maybe I'll get an idea

227
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,680
of what the male lead in the novel

228
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:50,000
would do

229
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,320
if the other person disappeared.

230
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:57,600
Does it have to follow
the formula that closely?

231
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,440
Today,

232
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:07,440
there aren't many customers
because Phatee isn't singing.

233
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,920
So I'm free.

234
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,080
Actually,

235
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:18,800
I'm wondering if I should give up
and find a new male lead.

236
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,120
So?

237
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,040
Did you find one?

238
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,760
But I might have to switch
from sweet romance

239
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,080
to another genre.

240
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,440
Like

241
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,480
something

242
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:38,600
with a warning.

243
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:40,440
NSFW or something.

244
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,440
Someone once told me

245
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,720
if I can't write the story
I want right now,

246
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,320
I should write something else
in the meantime.

247
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,520
Adult fiction

248
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,720
isn't so bad.

249
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,240
What kind

250
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,240
of adult fiction?

251
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,040
Murder?

252
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,040
Probably not.

253
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:20,320
Want to have some fun with adult fiction?

254
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:24,800
I'm not hiring you for this.

255
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,120
I'm just asking if you're interested.

256
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,400
So?

257
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,680
Interesting enough?

258
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,680
Well, fortune teller? Your client asked.

259
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:30,560
So, is Vann secretly seeing someone else?

260
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:34,200
He doesn't have someone else, right?

261
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,840
I'm sure he doesn't.

262
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:39,840
But he's so handsome.
Someone might approach him.

263
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,160
I've already gone through three decks.

264
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:44,640
Hey, listen to me.

265
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:50,000
Vann doesn't have the time or
the means to find someone else.

266
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,960
I believe you.

267
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,440
I just want to be sure.

268
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,920
Want to do a fourth deck, fortune teller?

269
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,880
We've gone through them all.

270
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:10,520
Mimi, what's wrong? You look so sad.

271
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:12,720
- Nay.
- What?

272
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:14,680
Stop reading cards for Vann and Rakkhun.

273
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,360
Do a love reading for me instead.

274
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:22,200
I'm hurt. Talay broke my heart.

275
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,520
Talay doesn't even allow you
to like him, Mimi.

276
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:29,440
The first rule of The Crow Club:

277
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,800
Anyone who works here can't like Talay.

278
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:37,280
But Talay can like the writer? Is that it?

279
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:41,360
Then should I just quit?

280
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:43,680
Then I can hit on Talay
without breaking the rules.

281
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,000
- What? What's wrong?
- Snap! Crack!

282
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,480
Snap! Boom!

283
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,600
Did you guys hear that strange sound?

284
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,960
What sound?

285
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,720
The sound of my heart.

286
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,760
Talay broke it.

287
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,800
If you weren't here,

288
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,320
I'd be hurt and lonely all by myself.

289
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:08,360
I'm lucky to have you hurting with me.

290
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:13,440
But you know, right? Once Talay goes home,

291
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,280
you'll have to watch the place
alone all night.

292
00:22:16,360 --> 00:22:18,720
- What? How can Talay go home?
- There.

293
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,320
- Hey!
- "Rule number one."

294
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,640
Talay.

295
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,560
Take my car.

296
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:28,800
Are we going to your place?

297
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:30,600
Who said you could?

298
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,800
Don't get your hopes up.

299
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,840
Why can't I go to your place?

300
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,520
What are you hiding?

301
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,800
I'm a romance novelist.

302
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:41,680
I never let anyone come over
except someone special to me.

303
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,640
And I'll…

304
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:46,000
probably never meet anyone.

305
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,680
Hey!

306
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,760
Talay.

307
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,080
Where are you going?

308
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,680
It's your shift today.

309
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:58,360
Why can't I go?

310
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,760
Well,

311
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:02,920
who's going to supervise
the delivery guys?

312
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,800
You're afraid to see the delivery guy.

313
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:10,000
Be brave, Tangmo.

314
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,680
You're just seeing your ex.

315
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,320
Want to put that in your novel?

316
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,560
A guy who is in denial

317
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,680
and keeps running into his ex,

318
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:20,920
who he's still not over.

319
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:22,680
What ex?

320
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,800
Just a friend.

321
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:26,400
No.

322
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,760
He's just someone I used to know.

323
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:30,160
That's all?

324
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,320
Then you can stay for the delivery.

325
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,040
Talay.

326
00:23:34,360 --> 00:23:38,160
Someone who won't admit how he feels
needs to be taught a lesson sometimes.

327
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:40,680
- I'm leaving.
- Hey.

328
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:42,040
Go ahead, Mr. Writer.

329
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:24,200
That's all.

330
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,240
You don't actually have to help me.

331
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:28,800
I'll carry it myself.

332
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,720
What? Who's helping you?

333
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,320
I'm not helping.

334
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,400
I'm just tired of waiting for you.
You're too slow.

335
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:37,880
You're so skinny and scrawny.

336
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:40,800
It'll take you till your next life
to finish carrying this stuff.

337
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:46,280
So that's the only reason.
You're not worried about me at all.

338
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:49,160
Right. When you're done,
bring me the bill.

339
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,960
Then you can finally leave.

340
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:08,640
What happened to your hand?

341
00:25:09,840 --> 00:25:11,280
Who did this to you? Tell me.

342
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:13,280
No one did anything to me.

343
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:16,680
I was just clumsy
doing delivery work this morning.

344
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:34,680
Stop taking delivery jobs,
delivering and carrying stuff.

345
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:36,600
Can you just focus on rehearsing with me?

346
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:40,360
If you're going to compete,
you can't treat your body like this.

347
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:42,480
Why do you care about me?

348
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:45,880
Yoyeh.

349
00:25:46,720 --> 00:25:49,920
You're the one who wants to win
that fucking reality show.

350
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:53,640
If you want to win,
focus on one thing at a time.

351
00:25:56,880 --> 00:26:00,000
But I need money
to survive until the competition, don't I?

352
00:26:01,480 --> 00:26:03,000
What if I give you that money?

353
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:06,520
Will you focus on rehearsing with me?

354
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:10,200
Give me your QR code.

355
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,200
You ran away from home to live alone.

356
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,480
Don't you need money too?

357
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:19,520
Give me your QR code.

358
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,520
I don't have money to throw around
like when I lived with Dad.

359
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:38,640
But it's not like I'm broke.

360
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:41,840
You can have last month's salary.

361
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:44,960
You still love splurging on people,
just like when you were a kid.

362
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:48,280
I'm not that little kid
who followed you around anymore.

363
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:50,600
I'm not splurging on you.

364
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:53,440
Consider it payment
for helping out at the shop.

365
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:56,680
Talay is too busy to help me anyway.

366
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:01,800
You haven't changed at all.
You always do things without asking me.

367
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:02,960
Are you insulting me?

368
00:27:03,040 --> 00:27:05,320
Then I take it back.
Transfer the money back to me.

369
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:06,480
No.

370
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:08,720
Your offer is good.

371
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:11,680
I'll help out at your shop instead.

372
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:13,200
But I want to be paid daily.

373
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,640
BALANCE: 3,259.50 BAHT

374
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:30,000
Damn it.

375
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:31,920
Shit, I've only got 3,000 baht left.

376
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:48,760
You're back late.

377
00:27:48,840 --> 00:27:50,960
Linda said you'd finish work
in the evening.

378
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:54,680
You must've enjoyed being
a paid companion.

379
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:57,800
Want to take over Vann's jobs, then?

380
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:59,040
No.

381
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:18,240
What the hell is wrong with you?

382
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:19,840
Standing there smiling to yourself.

383
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,520
Did Garlah's ghost possess you?

384
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:24,520
No.

385
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:27,440
Something's weird about you.

386
00:28:27,520 --> 00:28:28,640
You're not acting normal.

387
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:31,560
Fortune teller!

388
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:33,280
Read his fortune.

389
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:34,600
See who put a spell on him.

390
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,080
Let's do it, Bro.

391
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:38,160
Come here. Let's read your fortune.

392
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:41,320
We'll know once I draw the cards.

393
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:51,960
No one's put a spell on you.

394
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:53,400
But lately,

395
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:56,920
it looks like you'll encounter
something that

396
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,600
makes your heart flutter.

397
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,320
His heart will flutter?

398
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,800
Well?

399
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:05,080
Anything you want to tell me?

400
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:07,280
Maybe it'll cheer me up too.

401
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:10,720
No.

402
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:13,640
You sure?

403
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,360
Yeah.

404
00:29:16,600 --> 00:29:18,280
If I ask you about love,

405
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:19,600
could you even answer me?

406
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:21,600
You brat. You're fine when you're quiet,

407
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:23,160
but when you talk,
you always pick a fight.

408
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:25,160
Why did you decide to take the job?

409
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:27,120
Because you like him, right?

410
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:34,400
If you don't want to see your ex,
you shouldn't have taken the job.

411
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:37,600
Who the fuck started saying he's my ex?

412
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,600
Linda and Mimi.

413
00:29:41,200 --> 00:29:43,800
I know. I wasn't really asking you.

414
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:48,000
And I took that job

415
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:50,360
because I just wanted to sort out
my feelings from the past

416
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:52,200
and not leave them unresolved.

417
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,520
As for him,

418
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,320
whatever he thinks
is his fucking business.

419
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:58,520
I only care about my own outcome.

420
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,680
What if it turns out worse than before?

421
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:03,040
- What will you do?
- You brat!

422
00:30:03,120 --> 00:30:04,800
Do I look that stupid to you?

423
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:06,720
Take a good, long look at my face.

424
00:30:06,800 --> 00:30:08,760
I'm actually smart.

425
00:30:09,920 --> 00:30:11,040
Mm.

426
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,800
You'll know when the time comes.

427
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:17,880
And remember, some opportunities,
if we don't seize them,

428
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:21,720
they won't come again.

429
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:50,320
There's one more song, Kao.

430
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:52,240
It's pop rock.

431
00:30:52,320 --> 00:30:54,680
It's fun, easy on the ears,
and super catchy.

432
00:30:54,760 --> 00:30:55,920
Here.

433
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,320
No need. I have another meeting.

434
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:03,280
Kao, but the song's only two
or three minutes long.

435
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:09,080
Ranne, I'll be honest.

436
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:11,080
I don't think your band
can go on like this.

437
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:15,920
Shit.

438
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:18,320
Feels like getting dumped.

439
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:21,280
Of course. They're about to disband us.

440
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,480
Kao, please wait.

441
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:26,640
Kao!

442
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:29,480
Please give us one more chance.

443
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:32,080
We're working on a new song right now.

444
00:31:32,160 --> 00:31:33,480
- Right?
- Yeah.

445
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:35,360
A new song with a whole new sound.

446
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:37,480
You'll definitely hear it next week.

447
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,360
Enough.

448
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:43,080
I think we've been going in circles
for way too long.

449
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:46,040
And it still hasn't clicked.

450
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,720
The music needs a turning point.

451
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:50,120
I think this is where we end.

452
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:52,600
We'll definitely have
that turning point, Kao.

453
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:55,160
I'm trying to get a new member
to join the band.

454
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:57,880
I guarantee this person
can complete our band.

455
00:31:57,960 --> 00:32:00,680
Where are they?
If you've got someone, show me.

456
00:32:03,840 --> 00:32:05,200
Sorry, Kao.

457
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:07,720
Someone's here to audition.

458
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,880
He said Ranne told him to come here.

459
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:12,360
Who?

460
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:13,840
He said his name is Phatee.

461
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:21,080
This is the guy, Kao.
Our band's turning point.

462
00:32:23,360 --> 00:32:24,560
Really?

463
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:25,920
Then go get him.

464
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,000
Okay.

465
00:32:27,600 --> 00:32:29,080
Who the hell is he?

466
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:30,080
Yeah.

467
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:31,720
You'll meet him soon enough.

468
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:46,640
Yes.

469
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:48,120
You can introduce yourself.

470
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:50,360
Okay.

471
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:52,480
Hi, I'm Phatee.

472
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:58,400
That's it?

473
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:05,400
I play guitar and sing at a club too.

474
00:33:07,960 --> 00:33:09,960
Can you write songs too?

475
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,440
A little.

476
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:15,480
"A little."

477
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:18,400
Let me see your basic dance moves first.

478
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:22,000
Okay.

479
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:30,200
Is there a problem?

480
00:33:32,480 --> 00:33:33,560
No.

481
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:40,840
Wow.

482
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:43,040
Come on. I'll count you in.

483
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:47,960
Come on. I'll count you in.

484
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:49,000
Okay, start.

485
00:33:49,080 --> 00:33:51,080
One, two, three,

486
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:54,200
four, five, six, seven, eight.

487
00:33:54,280 --> 00:33:56,760
One, two, three, four,

488
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:59,120
five, six, seven, eight.

489
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,639
I think I've seen enough of your dancing.

490
00:34:10,719 --> 00:34:14,000
So, can you try singing?

491
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,840
Can you stop pacing?

492
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:32,320
I'm nervous.

493
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:35,639
Look at this.

494
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:38,199
It says we only have a 10%
chance of debuting.

495
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:40,800
By "it," you mean AI, right?

496
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,480
Can you stop believing it so much?

497
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:43,719
Have some confidence.

498
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:45,120
Stay calm like Saw.

499
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:46,840
Seriously?

500
00:34:47,639 --> 00:34:48,920
That's not staying calm.

501
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,560
That's running away from the problem.

502
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:00,960
Are you ready?

503
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,400
If you're ready, you can start.

504
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:18,000
Are you going to sing
with your back to the audience?

505
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:22,840
Turn around.

506
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:34,120
Go ahead.

507
00:35:48,520 --> 00:35:49,440
Excuse me,

508
00:35:50,040 --> 00:35:51,080
Kao.

509
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:52,400
Can I sing with him?

510
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:54,280
Because if we end up in the same band,

511
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,680
we'll have to sing together anyway.

512
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:59,040
Go ahead. Do whatever you want.
I've only got five minutes left.

513
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:00,440
Thank you.

514
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:06,560
Give it your all.

515
00:36:08,160 --> 00:36:09,920
You can sing the song
you sing at the club.

516
00:36:11,040 --> 00:36:12,440
But it's not finished yet.

517
00:36:12,520 --> 00:36:13,960
Just sing what you have.

518
00:36:14,720 --> 00:36:15,880
Trust me.

519
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:25,480
Then, please play the backing track.

520
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:27,520
Okay.

521
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:36,080
You can look at me.

522
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:02,640
<i>My world looks so dark and gloomy</i>

523
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:07,960
When people stare, I just crumble
So I run away

524
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:14,440
<i>Far from the crowd, just me, oh, no</i>

525
00:37:15,160 --> 00:37:18,840
<i>I try not to feel anything</i>

526
00:37:18,920 --> 00:37:23,080
<i>But my heart never listens</i>

527
00:37:23,160 --> 00:37:27,840
<i>I can't bear it</i>
<i>The sound of my heart's been so loud</i>

528
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:30,640
<i>Ever since you came</i>

529
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:35,160
<i>Too scared to say I love you</i>

530
00:37:35,240 --> 00:37:39,080
<i>Just being near you is enough</i>

531
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:42,920
<i>I wouldn't dare to get closer to you</i>

532
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:49,200
<i>But what can I do? I'm in love with you</i>

533
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:53,320
<i>- Should I shout it out?</i>
<i>- I wouldn't dare</i>

534
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:56,240
<i>I wouldn't dare</i>

535
00:37:57,160 --> 00:38:04,040
<i>Can I whisper it softly</i>
<i>to your ear instead?</i>

536
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:10,320
Ranne, how did it go?

537
00:38:10,400 --> 00:38:11,400
Did he pass?

538
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:12,920
What did Kao say?

539
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:14,280
I have no idea.

540
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:16,640
As soon as we finished singing,
they all left.

541
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:24,520
I'm heading back.

542
00:38:24,600 --> 00:38:26,640
The job's done. You can pay Linda.

543
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:27,960
Wait.

544
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:30,720
Hold on.
Aren't you staying to hear the result?

545
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:32,960
Probably not necessary.

546
00:38:33,040 --> 00:38:35,400
I don't think anyone wants to
hear someone like me sing.

547
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:37,360
Who told you that?

548
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,920
The other day, the audience
was singing along with you.

549
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:42,520
Your voice moves anyone who hears it.

550
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:46,080
But singing for fun
and singing seriously aren't the same.

551
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:48,720
The audience probably wants to hear

552
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:52,920
someone who can sing, dance well,
and has more confidence than me.

553
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:55,880
That was so damn good, though.

554
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:58,560
Your voice and mine work so well together.

555
00:38:58,640 --> 00:38:59,760
Have some confidence.

556
00:39:02,560 --> 00:39:04,000
You haven't seen me dance.

557
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:11,600
Was it that bad?

558
00:39:14,720 --> 00:39:15,880
I'll get going.

559
00:39:32,200 --> 00:39:33,200
What do we do?

560
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:36,760
I don't know anymore.

561
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:45,720
Oh. Where did your friend go?

562
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:46,960
He left.

563
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:48,960
Why did he leave?

564
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:51,040
I rushed to get a trainee contract
for him to sign.

565
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:52,160
What?

566
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,520
What do you mean?

567
00:39:55,120 --> 00:39:56,720
With a voice that good

568
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:59,960
and chemistry this good
between you and Phatee,

569
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:01,480
I'd be stupid to let him go.

570
00:40:02,640 --> 00:40:06,080
Ranne. I found your band's selling point.

571
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,440
Hurry and bring your friend back.
Otherwise, your band won't get to debut.

572
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:15,000
Hell yeah! We've got a chance!

573
00:40:15,080 --> 00:40:16,160
Hurry!

574
00:40:29,520 --> 00:40:31,280
I don't think we're going to debut.

575
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,080
Hey.

576
00:40:33,160 --> 00:40:35,400
Have some hope. Hope. Can you spell it?

577
00:40:36,240 --> 00:40:37,280
I can.

578
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:39,440
But how are you going to
convince an introvert like him

579
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:41,440
to get onstage with us?

580
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,320
Hey, Ranne.

581
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:46,280
You hired him to audition.

582
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:49,320
Why not hire him
to be a trainee at our label?

583
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:50,640
Right.

584
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:52,200
That's a good idea.

585
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,160
I…

586
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:56,880
I'm out of money.

587
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:00,920
Okay, Bro. I'm going home then.

588
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,280
- Stop.
- Calm down.

589
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:03,840
Sit down.

590
00:41:05,560 --> 00:41:06,600
Listen to me.

591
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:08,480
I won't give up.

592
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:11,440
At my age, I can't wait.

593
00:41:12,040 --> 00:41:15,400
If I don't debut this time,
I probably never will.

594
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,120
No matter what,

595
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:18,400
I

596
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:21,160
will find a way to get Phatee

597
00:41:21,240 --> 00:41:22,520
to join our band.

598
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:23,720
How?

599
00:41:41,320 --> 00:41:42,920
You're Phatee, right?

600
00:41:45,000 --> 00:41:46,520
You sing really well.

601
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:48,920
Can I take a photo with you?
Before you get famous and I can't.

602
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:53,880
Smile, please.

603
00:41:55,600 --> 00:41:56,520
Thank you.

604
00:41:59,520 --> 00:42:02,120
Phatee. You're famous now.

605
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:05,120
You still don't know, do you?

606
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:08,000
You've cut yourself off
from the outside world,

607
00:42:08,080 --> 00:42:10,680
so you don't know
what's going on out there.

608
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:13,320
Look at this.

609
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:17,600
Shit!

610
00:42:18,440 --> 00:42:19,720
This is just one clip.

611
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:21,280
It's got millions of views.

612
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:24,640
When you get famous,
don't forget about me.

613
00:42:24,720 --> 00:42:26,680
I'll even take out the trash for you.

614
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:29,880
I can't believe my brother's
going to be a famous singer.

615
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:31,280
No need.

616
00:42:33,160 --> 00:42:35,600
No need. By tomorrow,
everyone will have forgotten.

617
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:39,200
Aren't you going to build on this?

618
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:41,680
The opportunity is right in front of you.

619
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:42,600
Hey.

620
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:46,920
- No.
- What?

621
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:50,400
Then why--

622
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:56,920
A cloth used to wipe down a famous singer

623
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,280
would definitely sell at auction.

624
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:20,880
<i>I know you're happy when you sing.</i>

625
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:22,920
<i>If you change your mind</i>
<i>about signing the contract,</i>

626
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:24,640
<i>you can come see me.</i>

627
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:25,720
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

628
00:43:57,600 --> 00:43:59,640
What song should
we play this Valentine's Day?

629
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:02,240
- Hey, Ble.
- I--

630
00:44:04,400 --> 00:44:06,560
Play this song at the school event for me.

631
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:07,720
I like it.

632
00:44:12,040 --> 00:44:13,480
But I can't play this song.

633
00:44:14,080 --> 00:44:16,280
Then practice it for me.

634
00:44:16,360 --> 00:44:17,600
Help me out.

635
00:44:17,680 --> 00:44:19,160
I really want this song
at the school event.

636
00:44:23,200 --> 00:44:25,160
Fine! I'll try.

637
00:44:25,240 --> 00:44:26,800
Great. I'm off.

638
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:29,360
I can't play it.

639
00:44:29,440 --> 00:44:30,920
Can you?

640
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:32,680
I can't either. What song is this?

641
00:44:32,760 --> 00:44:34,040
Then who can we get to play it?

642
00:44:34,640 --> 00:44:35,560
Hey.

643
00:44:36,360 --> 00:44:37,360
I'll figure out the chords for you.

644
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:41,800
Great. Thanks for helping.

645
00:44:41,880 --> 00:44:43,120
- Thanks.
- Let's go.

646
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:58,760
SECRET - PAUSE

647
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:09,880
<i>I’ve been looking at you for so long</i>

648
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:12,920
<i>I don't dare to look</i>

649
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:16,000
<i>I always have to avoid your eyes</i>

650
00:46:16,080 --> 00:46:20,480
<i>I’m afraid that one day</i>

651
00:46:20,560 --> 00:46:24,040
<i>If you find out</i>

652
00:46:24,120 --> 00:46:27,640
<i>The truth I’ve been hiding away</i>

653
00:46:29,200 --> 00:46:34,600
<i>The secret I’ve hidden</i>
<i>I’ve never told anyone</i>

654
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:39,080
<i>I don't think I can hold it back anymore</i>

655
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:38,560
SONGBOOK

656
00:47:41,680 --> 00:47:46,360
RANNE

657
00:47:59,960 --> 00:48:04,320
RANNE

658
00:48:26,880 --> 00:48:28,680
Your friend still
hasn't gotten back to you?

659
00:48:31,080 --> 00:48:32,080
Not yet.

660
00:48:35,040 --> 00:48:36,680
Then I guess we're all on the same page.

661
00:48:37,880 --> 00:48:40,480
Tomorrow, I'll debut a new boy group.

662
00:48:41,240 --> 00:48:44,920
Anyway, thank you for all your hard work.

663
00:48:46,120 --> 00:48:47,800
I hope in the future,

664
00:48:47,880 --> 00:48:51,400
you'll find your own way
to keep pursuing your dreams.

665
00:48:54,920 --> 00:48:56,000
Here.

666
00:48:56,080 --> 00:48:58,240
Sign the trainee
contract termination papers,

667
00:48:58,960 --> 00:49:00,920
and you'll be free.

668
00:49:14,320 --> 00:49:15,560
I'll sign first.

669
00:49:16,520 --> 00:49:17,840
Let's get this over with.

670
00:49:20,520 --> 00:49:21,520
Ranne!

671
00:49:31,840 --> 00:49:32,840
You!

672
00:49:33,720 --> 00:49:35,720
I agree to become a trainee

673
00:49:36,680 --> 00:49:38,720
and debut with your band.

674
00:49:58,000 --> 00:49:59,800
Thanks for trusting me.

675
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:04,240
Thank you for doing this for our dream.

676
00:50:12,160 --> 00:50:16,160
Does this mean we get to keep going?

677
00:50:17,760 --> 00:50:19,120
Yeah. We do!

678
00:50:20,040 --> 00:50:21,960
- Really?
- We get to keep going!

679
00:50:22,040 --> 00:50:23,480
Really?!

680
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:26,920
- We can keep going!
- Keep going!

681
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:28,600
We'll get to debut!

682
00:51:23,840 --> 00:51:25,960
<i>Let's officially</i>
<i>introduce ourselves again.</i>

683
00:51:26,040 --> 00:51:29,560
This is Phatee.
He'll be A-Team's main vocalist.

684
00:51:33,720 --> 00:51:34,920
Whose song is this?

685
00:51:36,320 --> 00:51:38,720
<i>I was excited about the debut,</i>
<i>but now I'm starting to worry.</i>

686
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:40,200
I thought he'd at least
have the basics down.

687
00:51:40,280 --> 00:51:41,880
<i>He's clearly below zero.</i>

688
00:51:42,960 --> 00:51:44,080
<i>Thanks for working so hard.</i>

689
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:47,080
I'll stay by your side
and help push you forward.

690
00:51:47,880 --> 00:51:49,880
<i>You've always been my inspiration.</i>

691
00:51:51,400 --> 00:51:52,880
Did you know me before?
